---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import headshot from '../assets/edward-336.png';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Edward Jakunskas"
  description="Edward Jakunskas, Dublin. Computer vision and robotics engineer (research MSc, Maynooth). Since 2026 also an AI-native software engineer, delivering production systems by directing coding agents."
  path="/"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <Image src={headshot} width={168} height={168} alt="Edward Jakunskas" class="headshot" loading="eager" />
    <div>
      <h1>Edward Jakunskas</h1>
      <p class="tracks sans"><span>Computer vision &amp; robotics</span><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>AI-native software</span><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Dublin, Ireland</span></p>
      <p class="lede">Computer vision and robotics engineer, with a research MSc from Maynooth. Since 2026 also an AI-native software engineer: production systems delivered by directing coding agents.</p>
      <p class="links sans">
        <a href="https://github.com/Edward-VJ">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/edward-jakunskas/">LinkedIn</a>
        <a href="mailto:ejakunskas@gmail.com">Email</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="doors" aria-label="Two ways in">
    <a class="door" href="/work/">
      <span class="door-kicker sans">Read</span>
      <span class="door-title">The site</span>
      <span class="door-text">Work, research, the courtyard gallery, the cats, the CV, and how this site was built. Fast pages, no scripts.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="door" href="/play/">
      <span class="door-kicker sans">Play</span>
      <span class="door-title">The courtyard</span>
      <span class="door-text">Walk a courtyard with seven stations and seven hidden cats. Two games: scan a dark room, and pong against a PID controller you tune.</span>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="build-note">
    <p>This site is being built step by step from a public plan, and every commit carries the step it belongs to. Step PS-2 of 9 is the design system and shell you are looking at. <a href="/how-this-was-built/">How this was built</a>.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; align-items: start; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .headshot { border-radius: 8px; width: 168px; height: 168px; }
  .tracks { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.35rem 0.6rem; margin: -0.25rem 0 0.9rem; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); }
  .tracks .sep { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 400; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .links a { margin-right: 1.25rem; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .headshot { width: 120px; height: 120px; } }
  .doors { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
  .door { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink); }
  .door:hover, .door:focus-visible { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .door-kicker { font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); }
  .door-title { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.15; }
  .door-text { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.98rem; }
  .build-note { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 1rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
</style>
